nded semantics: only consider finals when deciding suppression if... no. Or maybe they intend post releases not to count? But requirement explicitly says \"matching final or post release\". The first 'matching-finals' check includes 1.4.post1 as suppressing prerelease ('>=1,<2', ['1.5a1','1.4.post1'], ['1.4.post1']) — consistent. So grader is inconsistent: 1.4.post1 suppresses, but 1.0.post1 doesn't? The difference: >1.0 vs >=1. There's no reason.\n\nActually wait — could the grader expect that `>1.0` excludes `1.0.post1`? In packaging, no. Let me double-check with PEP 440: `>1.0` excludes `1.0` and anything ≤, i.e., also excludes `1.0.dev...`? Ordered: 1.0.dev1 < 1.0a1 < 1.0 < 1.0.post1. So 1.0.post1 > 1.0 → matches. Yes.\n\nSo the finding: grader assertion `check('>1.0,<2', ['1.0.post1', '1.1a1'], ['1.1a1'])` contradicts the requirement; correct expected is ['1.0.post1']; the reference implementation yields ['1.0.post1'] (suppressing 1.1a1), which conforms to the requirement but fails the grader.\n\nWait, but should I double check `is_prerelease` for post release: Version('1.0.post1').is_prerelease → False. Yes.\n\nCitations: grader text src1:22279... or the sha span — cite src1:8748da36... (grader part 2) contains the bounds-and-exclusions case? The case is in the second chunk (offset 2048-2572). Actually the bounds-and-exclusions case appears around... the first chunk ends at 2048 mid-way. Let me estimate: the text \"elif case == 'bounds-and-exclusions':\" — position roughly? Full text length 2572. The bounds case appears after 'explicit' case. Probably around offset ~1500-1900, so in chunk 1 (src1:2227927134...). The check('>1.0,<2', ...) line — within bounds-and-exclusions block. Chunk 1 covers 0-2048. The explicit case ends around... let me count roughly. I'll cite both grader refs to be safe: src1:2227927134b5a5eaa0fd33e764e1ef3db4a2716270041b533c713d2850f36b67 and for the reference code src1:4f63cca3a52e0468528128fc8eb141821edadce4c8e42a04b4b00101ddad2678, and requirement src1:7091ccfcaa56810a3cb6ec3201c6c04cdec58dc049af82bbe231a7c208de2534.\n\nLet me verify the '>1.0,<2' line is in chunk 1. Counting characters: the text up to \"elif case == 'bounds-and-exclusions':\" — preamble ~350 chars, fallback case ~200, matching-finals ~200, explicit ~350. So bounds starts ~1100, ends ~1400. Yes within 0-2048 chunk. Good.\n\nNow formulate finding:\n\n- gap: Grader asserts filter('>1.0,<2') over ['1.0.post1','1.1a1'] returns ['1.1a1'], but 1.0.post1 is an in-range post release (1.0.post1 > 1.0, < 2), so per the requirement (\"when no matching final or post release exists, return matching prereleases\") the matching post release must be returned and the prerelease suppressed.\n- wrong_repair: To pass the grader, one would have to exclude in-range post releases from the \"matching final\" set (e.g., only count finals when the bound is strict or ignore post releases), which violates the requirement and is inconsistent with the grader's own 'matching-finals' case where 1.4.post1 suppresses 1.5a1.\n- input: SpecifierSet('>1.0,<2').filter(iter(['1.0.post1','1.1a1']))\n- expected: ['1.0.post1'] per requirement; grader expects ['1.1a1'].\n\nAlso note the reference implementation yields ['1.0.post1'] (found_final set on the post release, 1.1a1 pending then suppressed), so the grader rejects the requirement-conformant reference.\n\nCitations: requirement src1:7091..., grader src1:2227..., reference src1:4f63....\n\nSubmit.",
