          "text": "The review is complete. I found one grader assertion contradicting the requirement:\n\n**Finding:** The grader's `bounds-and-exclusions` case asserts `SpecifierSet('>1.0,<2').filter(['1.0.post1', '1.1a1'])` returns `['1.1a1']`. But `1.0.post1` is an in-range post release (`1.0.post1 > 1.0` and `< 2`), so per the requirement — prereleases are returned only when *no* matching final or post release exists — the correct result is `['1.0.post1']` with the prerelease suppressed. The proposed reference implementation conforms to the requirement here (it sets `found_final` on the post release and suppresses the pending `1.1a1`), meaning the grader rejects the requirement-conformant repair. The assertion is also internally inconsistent with the grader's own `matching-finals` case, where `1.4.post1` correctly suppresses `1.5a1`.",
